# Dropped into a preview folder as .htaccess by the preview workflows, and by
# nothing else — deploy.yml never copies it, so the live page at /portfolio/
# keeps its own indexing. A preview is a near-duplicate of, or a study for, the
# live page, and two indexable copies means a search engine picks one of them
# with no say from us about which.
#
# X-Robots-Tag rather than a meta tag alone, because the header covers the
# assets too and cannot be missed by a crawler that does not run scripts.
#
# Guarded: this host has mod_headers, but an .htaccess naming a module that is
# not loaded is a 500 on the whole directory, and a preview that 500s is worse
# than one that gets indexed.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header always set X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow"
</IfModule>
